    "caption": "🤖 Atlas Assembly Could Shrink to an Hour\n\nA single Atlas currently takes about a day to assemble. Boston Dynamics wants to cut that to about an hour next year, and eventually to minutes.\n\nThe company keeps prototyping under one roof. It makes tight-tolerance parts and cuts gears in-house, letting engineers revise them with machinists and test changes on real hardware the same or next day. Production is also being tuned with robotic arms for assembly.\n\n📊@tech",
