      "AgACAgIAAyEFAAMBClOLWAACBRBq14SVULldCU5rL9F20pmCCajS0gAChCVrG3zmoEq-TjAbe7yqNwEAAwIAA3gAAz0E",
      "AgACAgIAAyEFAAMBClOLWAACBRFq14SVAmJHZQXHm7HvOQO2SllFBQAChSVrG3zmoEp9pROYXN-jvQEAAwIAA3gAAz0E"
    ],
    "caption": "🥽 GlassTENG Runs on Facial Motion\n\nThe prototype from Northwestern University uses thin flexible triboelectric nanogenerators. When skin touches and leaves a sensor, the materials exchange electrons and produce short electrical pulses. Tests involved 20 volunteers.\n\nThree sensors sit near the nose, temple, and ear. The system identified the wearer’s activity with 93.8% accuracy. Tooth tapping reached 99%, while jaw clenching reached 96%. Pulse readings differed from a chest sensor by 1.82 beats per minute on average, tested at rest on 10 people.\n\nThe glasses currently send data over Bluetooth to a smartphone or tablet. The team wants them to process signals on-device, such as detecting a clenched jaw and reminding the wearer to relax it.\n\n📊@tech",
